  "body": "Found during #2736.\n\n## What happens\n\nIn `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`, the Adaptive2D arm calls `adaptive(&pp)`. When `carry_need!` finds a dive into stock, the arm sets `pp.links.approach.material_top` and calls `adaptive(&pp)` again. The second call plans all passes again.\n\nThe HSM plan (`pocket_hsm`, `adaptive/*`) does not read `material_top`. Only the emit step and the trochoid fallback (`adaptive_troch.rs`) read it. Thus, on the HSM path, the second plan gives the same passes as the first plan.\n\n## Readings (release, box part of #2736, upright, `optimal_load` 0.5, before the #2736 fix)\n\n- First plan: 28.98 s. Second plan: 28.55 s. Total: 57.8 s.\n- After the #2736 fix, one plan takes about 10 s in release and 60 s in debug. The upright case still plans two times.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The carried-stock pass plans the passes one time and emits them two times, or the second plan is skipped where its result is the same.\n- The posted output does not change. A test compares the output before and after on a fixture with carried stock.\n- The trochoid fallback, which reads `material_top`, keeps its present result.\n",
